    {
        "content": "<p>cfallin opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15341\">PR #15341</a> from <code>cfallin:debug-readonly-apis</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Several APIs that only read a store's state take mutable access to it, which makes them unusable where only shared access is available, such as in an eventual record/replay/snapshot mechanism. Now that GC values can be read as <code>Unrooted</code> references, with only shared access, several more APIs can take <code>impl AsContext</code> instead of <code>impl AsContextMut</code>: getters on <code>Instance</code> for tables, memories, and globals; debug getters; the debug FrameHandle API; and <code>Func::to_raw</code> (which I'll use in tests in later PRs). To make the frame-handle bit work, we need internal locking for the <code>FrameDataCache</code> (which avoids re-parsing the frame table when frame handles are re-obtained at each debug event).</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 641449698,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1794978978
    },
